Overlay patch 0043: menu + HUD inside stereoscopic 3D — Gui split
(= reference 0034; VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK §2.7, read reference D-033).
The 3D path (0044) skips gui StartDraw/EndDraw entirely (the Metal
backend's ImGui NewFrame acquires the SCREEN drawable — a stall while the
window is hidden), so the menu would be unreachable in 3D. Split the
frame: a public build-once method that runs the ImGui frame WITHOUT the
backend NewFrame (the caller primes ImGui_ImplMetal against an eye
framebuffer instead) and skips DrawGame/viewport work (the menu
composites OVER the already-rendered eye images); the caller renders the
resulting draw data into BOTH eyes, then a finish method closes the frame
(EndFrame + CheckSaveCvars — the 2D CVar flusher lives in EndDraw, which
3D never runs).
Two adaptations vs reference 0034 (audit 2026-07-22):
1. The gSoh3DMode extern + Main-Game re-dock self-heal RETARGET to
   src/port/SpaghettiGui.cpp — the runtime Gui object is Ship::
   SpaghettiGui whose DrawMenu() OVERRIDE is the only DrawMenu that ever
   executes; patching LUS Gui::DrawMenu would be a silent no-op (the
   vacuous-A/B class). The build-frame method's DrawMenu() call needs no
   change — Gui::DrawMenu is virtual in this fork and dispatches down.
2. #ifdef __IOS__ guards on every body that references shell symbols —
   OUR macOS build builds the overlaid vendor and links no shell TU
   (the Ship of Harkinian port oracle builds pristine). Gui.h declarations stay
   unguarded (declaration-without-definition is oracle-safe).
Shell prerequisites (SohIos_PerfHud3DText, gSoh3DMenuToggleReq writer,
gSoh3DDbgMenu* definitions) are already in the synced SohIosShell.m.

